**Read:** [Manufacture of Organic Fine Chemicals, BREF OFC](../sources/Organic-Fine-Chemicals-BREF.lingua#r_0DH473049K4WX7HAAY1P7SDS3K), the entire applicable spent-material, solids and residual-management context; [Large Volume Inorganic Chemicals — Solids and Others Industry, BREF LVIC-S](../sources/Inorganic-Solids-and-Others-BREF.lingua#r_1M61GTSHDW8CPV4PNH48PTB4Y4), a complete relevant residue/recovery product case; [Common Waste Water and Waste Gas Treatment/Management Systems in the Chemical Sector, BREF CWW](../sources/Chemical-Sector-Water-and-Waste-BREF.lingua#r_3DD06XBCANC091G38HBZ4BX7Y9), the full sludge, residual-inventory and constituent-transfer methods.

Solid residuals can contain useful elements, reactive phases, retained liquid, contaminants and changing physical structures. A bulk assay or generic waste name cannot determine recovery response, stability, leaching or downstream compatibility. Characterization needs representative material, phase/speciation and the actual service history.

Spent catalysts, filter cakes, salts, sludges, fines and contaminated packaging follow different pathways. Washing, thermal treatment, chemical recovery or use elsewhere can change both useful constituents and residual obligations. Reuse is a technical claim requiring a real destination and specification, not merely relabeling an outlet.

Close target and consequential impurity accounts through recovery and the remaining material. Reactions can change chemical form and mobility without removing the element. Water, energy, consumables, equipment and maintenance of a recovery route belong in the same full comparison.

**Work:** reconstruct a complete public spent-material or solid-residue case using primary characterization and process methods. Independently trace two consequential constituents and compare a justified recovery/management alternative at equal useful outputs and remaining residual requirements. Explain which observation would discriminate a phase/chemical explanation from sampling or retained-liquid effects; use [Mineralogy and petrology — minerals, crystals, rock processes, and investigation](../../../../nature/earth/mineralogy-and-petrology/Mineralogy-and-petrology.lingua#r_44F7X6GPMW6ZSCCN6D71QSVKBN), [Mining and mineral engineering — extraction, processing, and continuing work](../../../engineering/mining-and-mineral-engineering/Mining-and-mineral-engineering.lingua#r_22HJPS3RTK5EX1J55YJP75PHYA) and [Metals and metallurgical production — feed, refining, structure, useful products, and recovery](../../../../ergon/materials/metals-and-metallurgical-production/Metals-and-metallurgical-production.lingua#r_59BDAQXT81552YF5F8TH4KQQH1) where their shared material knowledge is needed.

**Continue:** [Evaluate chemical recovery through actual selectivity, quality and continuing losses](Reagent-solvent-catalyst-recovery-and-closed-loop-limits.lingua#r_58CA7PDF4F2TMB6G0V7VBGCPQN).

